      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2016-11-29T19:14:43.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I've been trying to play some games in the Temple of Zhu Long, and I'm curious as to how Rites of Renewal works. &nbsp;Is it:</p><p>(a) &nbsp;If the heroes discard X cards in a *single* round, they can resurrect a fallen hero at the end of the environment turn; OR</p><p>(b) The heroes discard any number of cards they want every turn; once the total number of cards discarded over the course of the game reaches X, they can resurrect a fallen comrade at the end of the next environment turn.</p><p>I didn't want to go about discarding cards until I was sure how it worked.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:48:26.123Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 1,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 5.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 15893,
      "topic_slug": "temple-of-zhu-long-rites-of-revival-question",
      "display_username": "robb8888",
