      "raw": "<p>From the last sentence of the very last paragraph of the latest fireside chats:</p><p>&quot;<span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.399999618530273px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Suppose Sky-Scraper is incapacitated and has used the &ldquo;become a target&rdquo; incapacitated ability. If she is revived using Rites of Revival, the 1 HP indestructible target status is wiped, and she is her regular self at 8 HP with a 33 HP max and is fully destructible. Rites of Revival essentially resets the character, starting anew.&quot;</span></p><p>To me that means everything that the entire deck is restored as if the character was starting over. Full 40 cards regardless of where they may have been right before Revival activated.&nbsp;</p>",
